# TLS-terminating reverse proxy in front of EMQX's plaintext WebSocket
# listener (#119). Caddy over EMQX-native TLS: Caddy's automatic HTTPS
# (cert issuance + renewal via Let's Encrypt) needs zero coordination
# with EMQX - no shared cert-file volume, no reload-on-renewal hook, no
# restart cadence to get EMQX to pick up a renewed cert. EMQX keeps
# speaking plain `ws` on 8083 exactly as it already does; Caddy is the
# only thing that ever sees a TLS handshake.
#
# `localhost:8083`, not a container name: the Caddy container runs with
# `--network host` (see scripts/relay-redeploy.sh) so it shares the VM's
# network namespace directly - the same thing EMQX's own `-p 8083:8083`
# publish already exposes on that host.
relay.thrw.app {
	reverse_proxy localhost:8083
}
